<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 119 0 R
/T (Memory: iteration needs O\(one line\) \(measured peak 21,819 B\); read\(\) holds the whole file plus the split copy, O\(file size\) \(6,004,003 B\); readlines\(\) holds every line as a separate string \(4,086,854 B\). The file was 1,578,873 bytes, so read\(\) used about 3.8 times the file size. Whole-file reading is acceptable only for small files that must be read more than once or searched randomly.)
