/T (Why it is hidden: the typing error raises UnboundLocalError, a subclass of NameError and therefore of Exception. The broad handler catches it on every P line, pass discards it, and the loop carries on, so the program finishes normally with plausible but wrong numbers. That is worse than a crash because nobody knows to look for the fault.)
/E (Why it is hidden: the typing error raises UnboundLocalError, a subclass of NameError and therefore of Exception. The broad handler catches it on every P line, pass discards it, and the loop carries on, so the program finishes normally with plausible but wrong numbers. That is worse than a crash because nobody knows to look for the fault.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12]
