1707 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 140 0 R
/T (Measured \(all new numbers, worst case for the list\): n = 2,000: 0.0129 s vs 0.00016 s; 4,000: 0.0522 s vs 0.00037 s; 8,000: 0.2084 s vs 0.00082 s; 16,000: 0.8242 s vs 0.00169 s. Doubling n multiplies the list time by about 4 \(quadratic\) but the set time only by about 2 \(linear\). At 50,000 registrations per run the list version would need roughly 8 seconds for duplicate checking alone \(extrapolated, not measured\), against 0.3 s for the whole real program.)
/E (Measured \(all new numbers, worst case for the list\): n = 2,000: 0.0129 s vs 0.00016 s; 4,000: 0.0522 s vs 0.00037 s; 8,000: 0.2084 s vs 0.00082 s; 16,000: 0.8242 s vs 0.00169 s. Doubling n multiplies the list time by about 4 \(quadratic\) but the set time only by about 2 \(linear\). At 50,000 registrations per run the list version would need roughly 8 seconds for duplicate checking alone \(extrapolated, not measured\), against 0.3 s for the whole real program.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
