2342 0 obj
<<
/Title (Everything in onescript: no imports, the code simply runs from top to bottom \(organisation \(a\)\). Package import cost: the first import attendance.stats finds, compiles \(or loads cached bytecode\), and executes the module once: measured 0.755 ms and 13.1 KiB of allocated memory for the three sub-modules. Afterwards the module object is stored in sys.modules, so repeating the import is a dictionary lookup: 0.133 microseconds each. So import cost is a one-time O\(size of the code\) and O\(1\) afterwards, and the memory is small and constant \(each module is held once, however many files import it\).)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2321 0 R
/Next 2343 0 R
>>
endobj
2343 0 obj
<<
/Title (Finding and changing a function: in a single script of n lines you may scan O\(n\) lines \(53 here, and thousands in a real project\); in the package you go straight to attendance/stats.py \(16 lines\) because the function is named by its module. The time/space of the program itself is unchanged by the organisation; the benefit is human effort, testing and reuse, while the cost is a few more files and a sub-millisecond one-time import.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2321 0 R
/Prev 2342 0 R
/First 2366 0 R
/Last 2367 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
